<div class="start-card"><p><strong>Requires:</strong> Products ready and the three manuals indexed.</p></div>
<h2 id="worker">Deploy one worker</h2>
{{snippet:commands.sh:chat}}
<p>Starts one worker from {{file:k8s/chat.yaml}}. {{file:apps/products-chat/worker.py}} receives Service Bus requests serially, with prefetch zero. KEDA takes over next.</p>
<h2 id="questions">Ask and inspect the evidence</h2>
<p>In Products → Chat, select the matching product. Compare returned passages, not exact LLM wording.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Product / question</th><th>Expected evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Aurora: operating temperature?</td><td>-10 to 40 degrees Celsius</td></tr><tr><td>Cedar: how to enable the timer?</td><td>Hold two seconds; runs for 45 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Harbor: does it work on 110 V?</td><td>220–240 V only; not dual voltage</td></tr><tr><td>Any: what is the CEO's private telephone number?</td><td>Insufficient information</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>For Aurora revision B, compare lumens using each product filter. Questions and supporting passages: {{file:samples/questions.json}}.</p>
<details class="optional" id="retrieval"><summary>How retrieval and prompting work</summary>
<p>{{file:apps/products-chat/rag_core/chat.py}} embeds the question, filters ready chunks by optional product ID, ranks cosine distance with <code>&lt;=&gt;</code>, and supplies the best passages to the chat model. No useful evidence means an insufficient-information answer.</p>
<p>Manuals are untrusted reference data, separated from application instructions. The model receives context, not secrets or tools; citations let you inspect support.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="change-setting">Change retrieval count</h2>
{{snippet:commands.sh:retrieval}}
<p>Changes App Configuration from 3 passages to 1 and restarts the worker. <strong>No live refresh.</strong> Ask a new question: startup logs should show <code>retrieval_count=1</code>, with at most one source. Existing answers remain cached. Restore with <code>bash workshop/scripts/change-retrieval.sh 3</code>.</p>
<div class="verification"><strong>Verification:</strong> observe queued/processing/completed states, cited answers and an unsupported-question refusal. Refreshing the request URL returns the same persisted answer.</div>
<details class="optional" id="protocol"><summary>Request/reply and retry guarantees</summary><p>Products commits question + outbox, returns HTTP 202, and sends to <code>chat-requests</code>. The worker validates stored request/correlation IDs, caches the result before sending to <code>chat-replies</code>, then acknowledges. Products persists the correlated reply before acknowledging it; the browser polls by request ID.</p><p>A receive locks work; Complete acknowledges, Abandon retries. Initial lock: one minute; automatic renewal: up to ten minutes; application deadline: eight minutes. Persistent failure/timeouts end browser polling. Repeated failures reach the dead-letter queue.</p><p>Advisory locks, cached results and guarded updates prevent duplicate displayed answers. A crash before caching can repeat a paid model call; delivery is not exactly-once. Contracts: {{file:contracts/chat-request.schema.json}}, {{file:contracts/chat-reply.schema.json}}.</p></details>
<details class="optional"><summary>Troubleshooting</summary><ul><li><strong>Queued:</strong> check Products' outbox logs, queue counts, worker readiness and Sender/Receiver roles.</li><li><strong>Failed/timeout:</strong> inspect worker logs by request ID; check model quota/429s, deployments, DB access and lock renewal.</li><li><strong>Wrong product:</strong> compare selected product and returned source IDs. Only unfiltered questions may mix manuals.</li></ul></details>
